Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 01:05:19 -0400
Subject: let a tab be moved to another Space

Spaces could be made, switched and filled with new tabs, but a tab already open
could not be moved out of the one it was in. A Space's context menu now offers
to take the current tab.

Put there rather than in the tab's own context menu because that means no change
to TabStripModel's command enum or to tab_menu_model.cc, and because the target
is the thing being pointed at: right-click where the tab should go.

Disabled when there is nowhere to move to -- the tab is already in that Space --
and for pinned tabs, which are the essentials row and belong to every Space
already.

Moving switches to the target Space, so the tab stays in front of the user
rather than vanishing into a Space they are not looking at.

Why: without it a Space could only be filled going forward, and an arrangement
you already have could never be tidied into one.
Removable when: tabs can be dragged onto a Space icon, which is how the
reference does it.
